GeneralsX: AMD FidelityFX FSR 3.1 temporal upscaler, DXVK_UPSCALER=fsr3.
Built from the GLSL shaders and the Vulkan backend of the FidelityFX SDK
v1.1.4 (FSR 3.1.4), which the build copies to src/dxvk/fsr3/ffx-sdk; the
shaders are compiled with glslang into SPIR-V tables like FSR 2's. Without
the SDK, DXVK builds as before and DXVK_UPSCALER=fsr3 logs that FSR 3 is
unavailable and uses FSR 2. FSR 3 takes the same scene inputs as FSR 2
(camera motion from depth, jitter, reactive mask) and reuses the FSR 2
prepare and composite shaders, so the interface is taken from the EASU
image and never runs through the temporal upscaler. A shim hides device
extensions the backend would otherwise use (fp16 permutations are not
compiled) and defers the image view destruction of the backend until the
command list that used the views has completed. Log lines start with
[FSR3]; if FSR 3 fails, FSR 2 takes over, then FSR 1.0. The backend
gets the shim's vkGetDeviceProcAddr: with the device's own lookup,
vkGetBufferMemoryRequirements2KHR is NULL (DXVK uses the core function)
and the backend crashes creating its first context. The shim also hides
debug utils and AMD buffer marker functions DXVK does not enable, the
FSR 3 shaders are built with glslang -Os so that passes do not reference
descriptors the backend leaves unwritten, and sharpening, output format
and DXVK_FSR_TIMING work as for FSR 2.

